<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yonago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yonago is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori-prefecture">Tottori Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast near the border with Shimane, in the former province of Hoki. Its castle, completed in the early 17th century, was held under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori">Tottori</a> domain by the Arao family, senior retainers of the Ikeda lords, who governed Hoki on their behalf. It grew into the main commercial town of western Tottori.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yonago.jpg" alt="Yonago" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1,2,6 by 663highland, 3,4,5 by Lemon · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yonago_montage_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
